      en: "The BBVA Tower is a prominent skyscraper that defines the skyline of Panama City's financial district along Avenida Balboa. Known for its modern glass facade and strategic location overlooking the Pacific Ocean, it serves as the headquarters for one of the country's major banking institutions. The building is a symbol of Panama's status as a leading international financial center and its rapid urban growth over the last few decades. The area around the tower is a bustling hub of commerce, with many of the world's largest banks and corporations having offices nearby. The BBVA Tower is not only a functional office space but also a landmark of the 'Cinta Costera' waterfront, which has become a center for both business and leisure in the capital. Economics K8 — Panama as an international financial hub.",
